Highest-Value Optimizations

Hoist loop-invariant memory loads for frequently reused vars.
Repeated loads like MOV P0, 28672 / MOV P0, 288 and repeated TEXT address fetches inside loop body.
Estimated gain: ~3-8% runtime in hot loops, modest code-size reduction.

Implement real expression simplification pass (currently mostly placeholder).
ExpressionSimplifier.simplify_expression currently returns original expr with fixed cost estimate.
Add algebraic simplification + CSE-lite + constant propagation.
Estimated gain: ~4-10% instruction reduction, ~3-8% runtime.

Tighten live-range scheduler to basic-block scope only (or strict barriers).
Current scheduling is conservative but still global enough to risk subtle ordering issues.
Limit reordering to explicit basic blocks for safer wins.
Estimated gain: ~2-5% runtime, lower regression risk.


Pipeline Optimizations

Add --asm-only / --no-assemble mode in nobasic_compiler.py.
Skip assembler invocation during iteration or test loops.
Compile-time gain: typically ~30-70% faster edit-compile cycles for codegen-only work.

Add incremental compile cache keyed by source hash + flags.
Cache token stream/AST/semantic artifacts when unchanged.
Compile-time gain: ~40-80% on repeated runs in local iteration.

Add pass-level timing and counters in verbose mode.
Report instruction counts pre/post each pass and spill/load-store counts.
Not direct speedup, but improves optimization ROI quickly.


Recommended Priority Order

Peephole label/directive correctness fix (unblocks safe use of existing gains).
Direct branch lowering for comparisons/conditions.
Spill allocator correctness fix.
Loop-invariant load hoisting.
Real expression simplifier + pass metrics.